full listing committed beside this file as p2.s

== 1. the control: wrapping add, left against right ==
193:_wrap_right = _wrap_left
  the assembler ALIASES the two symbols to one body. LLVM proved wrapping
  addition associative and emitted the computation once. the control passes:
  the instrument can see a reassociation when one happens.

== 2. unsigned saturating add, left against right ==
-- sat_left first three instructions --
	and	w8, w0, #0xff
	add	w8, w8, w1, uxtb
	mov	w9, #255
-- sat_right first three instructions --
	and	w8, w2, #0xff
	add	w8, w8, w3, uxtb
	mov	w9, #255
  two distinct bodies. sat_left folds a,b first; sat_right folds c,d first.
  NOT aliased, NOT reassociated. so the backend does not have this law,
  and probe 1 proves exhaustively at 8 bits that the law is TRUE.

== 3. the reductions, where reassociation is what buys the vector form ==
  wrap_reduce      vector ops: 16
  sat_reduce       vector ops: 0
  sat_reduce_tree  vector ops: 15   of which uqadd.16b: 15

  sat_reduce is the scalar byte-at-a-time loop:
LBB1_1:
	ldrb	w11, [x0, x9]
	add	w8, w11, w8, uxtb
	cmp	w8, #255
	csel	w8, w8, w10, lo
	add	x9, x9, #1
	cmp	x9, #256

  sat_reduce_tree, the SAME computation with the reassociation written out:
	ldp	q0, q1, [x0]
	uqadd.16b	v0, v0, v1
	ldp	q1, q2, [x0, #32]
	uqadd.16b	v0, v0, v1
	uqadd.16b	v0, v0, v2
	ldp	q1, q2, [x0, #64]

== what this establishes ==
  the hardware instruction exists (uqadd.16b saturates sixteen lanes at once).
  the backend WILL use it once the reassociation is written explicitly.
  the backend will NOT perform that reassociation itself, at any of the four
  associativity sites above, although the law is true and probe 1 proves it.
  so a true law, held in the typestate and lost at lowering, is the whole of
  what stands between a byte-at-a-time loop and a sixteen-lane one.

== what this does NOT establish ==
  how much faster the vector form runs. no timing was taken, no harness was
  used, there are no competitor arms and no artifact trail. that question is
  UNPRICED and needs mock/benches/.
  and every sentence here is indexed to the toolchain and target printed at
  the top. it is a fact about this backend on this day, not about arithmetic.

  one further unexploited win, noted rather than pursued: the tail of
  sat_reduce_tree folds the sixteen lanes back scalar, sixteen dependent
  csel steps. a log-depth uqadd tree would do it in four.
